Huawei 4.14 map mmap candidate
=============================

Reference: LineageOS/android_kernel_google_msm-4.14
Pinned donor: bb17b7de4b570f2c0c32ddba0543cac03c58dd84

The exact donor patches in this directory preserve original author/trailer
history. They are reference imports, not applied whole-tree cherry-picks.
The following Huawei integration commit ports their ARRAY allocation and
map-fd/VMA behavior to the existing socket/verifier architecture, with these
explicit adaptations:

* Canonical BPF_F_MMAPABLE=0x400; ordinary ARRAY only. PERCPU and fd arrays
  reject it. Existing typed ARRAY BTF checking remains in force. Program
  readonly/writeonly flags remain rejected on ARRAY because their verifier
  contract is outside this candidate. Mmap nevertheless defensively rejects
  writable views of any future BPF_F_RDONLY_PROG map.
* User-mappable vmalloc uses existing __vmalloc_node_range with VM_USERMAP,
  zeroing, NUMA and no-retry allocation. No replacement of Huawei mm code.
* Value pages are separate from metadata, include zeroed padding, and have
  subtraction/page-based offset bounds (no overflowing vm_pgoff multiply).
* Map fd mmap dispatch is ops-based. Ringbuf may later use it without an ARRAY
  flag. SHARED required; executable views/upgrades rejected. The callback must
  preserve vm_file, VM_WRITE and VM_MAYWRITE accounting, and default vm_ops.
* File references owned by the VM keep map alive. No duplicate map references.
  Extra VMA open/close callbacks track MAYWRITE even after write->read mprotect.
* Freeze is deliberately ARRAY-only and syscall-side. It does NOT stop BPF
  program writes. Other map freeze types return EOPNOTSUPP. No readonly scalar
  tracking/verifier changes or new helper semantics are imported.
* Permission check and write-active registration share freeze_mutex. The mutex
  is released before copies, map callbacks or mmap. Failed mmap rolls back the
  registration and clears callbacks; failed syscall writes decrement once.
  This closes the old update/freeze TOCTOU without importing a newer verifier.
* Generic map_poll returns unsigned int (4.14 ABI), calls map_poll if present,
  otherwise POLLERR, following donor ringbuf introduction 7b594c703b26.

Host tests execute extracted production allocation/free/mapping, fd mmap/poll,
write begin/accounting, freeze and full update/delete syscall bodies. The host
substitutes structure declarations, allocation, fd, locks, atomic, RCU, usercopy,
VMA and remap services. Split/fork/fd-close and update/freeze interleavings are
sequential models. These tests are NOT real VM, page protection, SMP, RCU or
syscall tests; actual kernel mapping/lifetime behavior remains a runtime gate.
Production whole-file cross-compilation validates the real kernel declarations.
